{"name":"Citrus Punch","hex":"#fdea83","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"citrus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several shrubs or trees of the genus Citrus in the family Rutaceae.","The fruit of such plants, generally spherical, oblate, or prolate, consisting of an outer glandular skin (called zest), an inner white skin (called pith or albedo), and generally between 8 and 16 sectors filled with pulp consisting of cells with one end attached to the inner skin. Citrus fruits include orange, grapefruit, lemon, lime, and citron."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or similar to citrus plants or fruit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citrus"},{"term":"punch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hit or strike with one's fist.","A blow from something other than the fist."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike with one's fist.","To herd (cattle) as a cowboy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Citrus","blocks":[{"text":"Citrus is a genus of flowering trees and shrubs in the family Rutaceae. Plants in the genus produce citrus fruits, such as citrons, mandarins, and pomelos. Many important citrus crops have been developed through extensive hybridization, including oranges, lemons, grapefruits, and limes, all of which have many cultivars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/OrangeBloss_wb.jpg/330px-OrangeBloss_wb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/Ichangfruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/Ichangfruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File